{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794529388607,"sessionID":"ses_e2db80179ffeaOrYcgpmM7vbPY","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2496630002dh6d5pHrxNqpsK","sessionID":"ses_e2db80179ffeaOrYcgpmM7vbPY","messageID":"msg_1d24954810010n6ftAmU6a9bPO","type":"tool","id":"call_eca26ae069df4ebd8f644c16","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \"CARRY-003|standalone|scoring-compatibility\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/spec.md | head -40"},"output":"40:**Scope Boundary**: The public recommendation fields, the hook brief head, the degraded-path contract, the allow-list retirement and the hand-authored bridge leftovers. Scoring, the policies themselves, `AGENTS.md` and the runtime pointers stay as they are. The group labelled CARRY-003 holds three criteria phase 003 left unmet and can be kept or dropped as one unit.\n112:$ jq -c '[.python[].id | select(test(\"spec-kit\"))]' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json\n204:- CARRY-003: clear the typed `/create:agent` ambiguity, prove that a metadata command with no compatibility row is active and reach `/speckit:search` from the review's probe prompt.\n231:| `ADV/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json` | Modify | Four Python rows and one owner key deleted |\n236:| `ADV/lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json` | Modify | CARRY-003 (a) and (c) |\n237:| Tests under `ADV/tests/` | Create, Modify | Schema, golden briefs, degraded contract, old daemon, CARRY-003 (b) |\n273:### CARRY-003 - Criteria phase 003 left unmet (keep or drop as one group)\n277:| REQ-015 | CARRY-003 (a): the default command capture prints `[]` for `typed_same_owner_ambiguous`, with the pinned numbers unchanged. |\n278:| REQ-016 | CARRY-003 (b): `scoring-compatibility.json` lists no `command-spec-kit-plan`, `-complete`, `-implement` or `-resume` row, and a fixture test proves that a metadata command with no compatibility row is active in both runtimes. |\n279:| REQ-017 | CARRY-003 (c): `show me which packets mention the token cap` returns a passing entry with `command` `/speckit:search` and `policy` `run`, with false offers still 0 of 35. |\n308:| Risk | The CARRY-003 (a) fix changes ambiguity for other prompts | Med: the ambiguity count moves | The pinned capture is the gate, and the fix is reverted and marked blocked if it moves |\n310:| Risk | The CARRY-003 (c) phrase is written for a known probe prompt | Med: it scores that prompt and little else | The tune reach and false-offer counts must hold, and the group can be dropped as one unit |\n365:- Does CARRY-003 stay in this phase? Decision: yes, by the earlier answer \"Carry three, settle five (Recommended)\". Phase 003's ADR-017 points at this group.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"40:**Scope Boundary**: The public recommendation fields, the hook brief head, the degraded-path contract, the allow-list retirement and the hand-authored bridge leftovers. Scoring, the policies themselves, `AGENTS.md` and the runtime pointers stay as they are. The group labelled CARRY-003 holds three criteria phase 003 left unmet and can be kept or dropped as one unit.\n112:$ jq -c '[.python[].id | select(test(\"spec-kit\"))]' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json\n204:- CARRY-003: clear the typed `/create:agent` ambiguity, prove that a metadata command with no compatibility row is active and reach `/speckit:search` from the review's probe prompt.\n231:| `ADV/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json` | Modify | Four Python rows and one owner key deleted |\n236:| `ADV/lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts`, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json` | Modify | CARRY-003 (a) and (c) |\n237:| Tests under `ADV/tests/` | Create, Modify | Schema, golden briefs, degraded contract, old daemon, CARRY-003 (b) |\n273:### CARRY-003 - Criteria phase 003 left unmet (keep or drop as one group)\n277:| REQ-015 | CARRY-003 (a): the default command capture prints `[]` for `typed_same_owner_ambiguous`, with the pinned numbers unchanged. |\n278:| REQ-016 | CARRY-003 (b): `scoring-compatibility.json` lists no `command-spec-kit-plan`, `-complete`, `-implement` or `-resume` row, and a fixture test proves that a metadata command with no compatibility row is active in both runtimes. |\n279:| REQ-017 | CARRY-003 (c): `show me which packets mention the token cap` returns a passing entry with `command` `/speckit:search` and `policy` `run`, with false offers still 0 of 35. |\n308:| Risk | The CARRY-003 (a) fix changes ambiguity for other prompts | Med: the ambiguity count moves | The pinned capture is the gate, and the fix is reverted and marked blocked if it moves |\n310:| Risk | The CARRY-003 (c) phrase is written for a known probe prompt | Med: it scores that prompt and little else | The tune reach and false-offer counts must hold, and the group can be dropped as one unit |\n365:- Does CARRY-003 stay in this phase? Decision: yes, by the earlier answer \"Carry three, settle five (Recommended)\". Phase 003's ADR-017 points at this group.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \\\"CARRY-003|standalone|scoring-compatibility\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/spec.md | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1794529388080,"end":1794529388607}}}}
