{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794529394991,"sessionID":"ses_e2db80179ffeaOrYcgpmM7vbPY","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2497c20002h779M14tDEfVUB","sessionID":"ses_e2db80179ffeaOrYcgpmM7vbPY","messageID":"msg_1d24970cc0015Z8Oj7IKx50L3w","type":"tool","id":"call_57b88920d8dc4df891f4b8a1","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -rn \"no compatibility row|compatibility row|activateStandalone|standalone skill\" specs/system-skill-advisor --glob '*.md' | head -30"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/codebase-conformance/002-advisor-test-drift/002-advisor-suite-drift-reconciliation/implementation-summary.md:The parity subset left red in August was resumed once the surfaces that feed the scorer had settled. The compiled skill graph was recompiled with its own compiler: the node set is identical except that `sk-design-md-generator`, now a mode of the `sk-design` hub, is no longer a n, six skills carry more signals, and the one topology warning is gone. On that graph the corpus parity test reports the Python reference making 114 gold-correct calls (was 112) and the native scorer preserving 108 of them (was 107), so both frozen numbers moved upward and were re-frozen. The divergence ledger was regenerated with its capture tool: two new divergences added, three resolved ones removed, three changed ones re-approved, each with a reason written after reading the prompt. One native move is a regression against gold, a documentation-consistency audit that native routes to sk-doc; it is recorded in the corpus test's accepted list and the ledger rather than hidden. `skill-advisor-cli-parity` and `advisor-graph-health` pass without change.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:| Q013 | Amend the sk-create-skill contract so a n may carry command-metadata.json. | Not stated. | None | 002 plan.md, sk-create-skill skill-root-metadata-contract |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:LOGIC-SYNC REQUIRED while planning phase 002. The review says to add a command-metadata.json to system-spec-kit (7 /speckit commands) and sk-prompt (/prompt:improve). But the repo's skill root metadata contract forbids that file on ns, and both are standalone (the gate passes 14 of 14 today and would fail). Where should the risk class for these 8 commands live?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/spec.md:- CARRY-003: clear the typed `/create:agent` ambiguity, prove that a metadata command with n is active and reach `/speckit:search` from the review's probe prompt.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/spec.md:| REQ-016 | CARRY-003 (b): `scoring-compatibility.json` lists no `command-spec-kit-plan`, `-complete`, `-implement` or `-resume` row, and a fixture test proves that a metadata command with n is active in both runtimes. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/spec.md:**Key Decisions**: amend the skill root metadata contract so a n may carry `command-metadata.json` (operator decision, 2026-11-12), emit policies as a new top-level key so no bridge entry and no scorer input changes\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/codex-luna/deep-research-strategy.md:### Treating command-file presence as proof of an eligible route; projection has explicit disabled states, and ns can diverge by runtime identity. -- BLOCKED (iteration 2, 1 attempts)\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/codex-luna/deep-research-strategy.md:- What was tried: Treating command-file presence as proof of an eligible route; projection has explicit disabled states, and ns can diverge by runtime identity.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/codex-luna/deep-research-strategy.md:- Do NOT retry: Treating command-file presence as proof of an eligible route; projection has explicit disabled states, and ns can diverge by runtime identity.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/codex-luna/deep-research-strategy.md:- Treating command-file presence as proof of an eligible route; projection has explicit disabled states, and ns can diverge by runtime identity. (iteration 2)\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/tasks.md:- [ ] T042 [P] CARRY-003 (b): in `$ADV/tests/command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts`, add a case that builds a fixture skills root through the file's existing fixture seam with one n whose `command-metadata.json` declares a command that `scoring-compatibility.json` does not list, and asserts the derived entry is enabled for both `typescript` and `python`. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/implementation-summary.md:The 8 commands that had no attributes anywhere now have them: `system-spec-kit` and `sk-prompt` each carry a `command-metadata.json`, which the skill root metadata contract now permits on a n when each entry names the skill itself as owner. The policies are a new top-level list in the generated file. Nothing scores on them yet, and no bridge was switched on or off.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/codex-luna/iterations/iteration-002.md:- Treating command-file presence as proof of an eligible route; projection has explicit disabled states, and ns can diverge by runtime identity.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/codex-luna/iterations/iteration-002.md:- Contradictory evidence: Bridge README says id equals inventoryId for ns, but the Python deep-research row differs.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/codex-luna/iterations/iteration-007.md:4. Bridge identity and ownership are assembled from three source families: skill command-metadata, allow-list ns, and doctor routes whose skill_agent tags supply skill and mode. The deriver validates these separately. This supports normalizing to one command catalog; the three distinct authorities contradict choosing any one current source as complete coverage. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md:16-29] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md:54-64] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs:98-108] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs:125-135]\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/codex-luna/iterations/iteration-007.md:5. The generated /deep:research bridge's parent skillId is system-deep-loop and ownerMode research; its Python n instead carries id command-spec-kit-deep-research and owningSkill deep-research. The metadata choreography explains that parent-to-leaf relationship. Keep canonical command id, parent skill, leaf workflow and runtime alias as distinct fields; the existing runtime row's differing id values contradict flattening these into one owner id. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json:319-340] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs:557-558]\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/codex-luna/deep-research-dashboard.md:- Treating command-file presence as proof of an eligible route; projection has explicit disabled states, and ns can diverge by runtime identity. (iteration 2)\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/plan.md:- **Activation by construction**: `runtimeCompatibility` (`derive-command-bridges.cjs:652-686`) enables a non-doctor metadata command with no hub mode without a n, and fills `order` and the Python slash markers by default.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/tasks.md:- [ ] T027 Enable a non-doctor metadata command by construction in `runtimeCompatibility`, with a default `order` and default Python slash markers (`$D`). Verify: a fixture case in `tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` with a metadata command and n reports the command active, and `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`. Not met as written: activation by construction works for the 8 standalone commands, but the fixture case in `tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` does not exist.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/acceptance-criteria.md:| AC-011 | REQ-011 | Given a metadata command with n, When the deriver runs, Then the command is active, and the compatibility file holds no row for the 8 non-hub commands | Activation by construction works for the 8 standalone commands, but `scoring-compatibility.json` still lists `command-spec-kit-plan`, `-complete`, `-implement` and `-resume` in its `python` list, and the planned fixture case does not exist. Re-measured on 2026-11-12: the four ids are still in the `python` list and the fixture case is 