-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/tasks.md:- [ ] T027 Enable a non-doctor metadata command by construction in `runtimeCompatibility`, with a default `order` and default Python slash markers (`$D`). Verify: a fixture case in `tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` with a metadata command and n reports the command active, and `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`. Not met as written: activation by construction works for the 8 standalone commands, but the fixture case in `tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` does not exist.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/acceptance-criteria.md:| AC-011 | REQ-011 | Given a metadata command with n, When the deriver runs, Then the command is active, and the compatibility file holds no row for the 8 non-hub commands | Activation by construction works for the 8 standalone commands, but `scoring-compatibility.json` still lists `command-spec-kit-plan`, `-complete`, `-implement` and `-resume` in its `python` list, and the planned fixture case does not exist. Re-measured on 2026-11-12: the four ids are still in the `python` list and the fixture case is still missing. Phase 005 carries this row in CARRY-003 (ADR-017) | Superseded | ADR-017 |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/003-doctor-command-surfacing/002-doctor-command-routing/review/lineages/deepseek-max/evidence/pre/SKILL.md:# This n emits exactly one workflow mode. Every routed leaf is a\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/z_archive/004-skill-graph/002-skill-graph-daemon-native-advisor-tools/research/iterations/iteration-024.md:- `.opencode/specs/system-spec-kit/026-graph-and-context-optimization/009-hook-package/002-skill-graph-daemon-and-advisor-unification/research/deep-research-strategy.md:111` → D1 evidence asks for `ls -R` inventory of n-advisor vs MCP-side skill-advisor, SQLite DB location, and test files.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/z_archive/004-skill-graph/002-skill-graph-daemon-native-advisor-tools/research/iterations/iteration-024.md:- **Rationale:** Adopt this split inventory as the canonical baseline for Track D: the live graph and hook/runtime shell already live in system-spec-kit MCP, while the scoring brain, JSON fallback, CLI health, regression, and benchmark harnesses remain in the n-advisor package.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/z_archive/004-skill-graph/002-skill-graph-daemon-native-advisor-tools/research/research.md:| D1 Current split inventory | `adopt_now` | high | Treat the split inventory as the migration baseline: system-spec-kit MCP owns live graph and hook shell; n-advisor owns Python scoring, JSON fallback, CLI health, regression, and benchmark harnesses. | `iterations/iteration-024.md:6`, `iterations/iteration-024.md:48`, `iterations/iteration-024.md:68` |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -rn \\\"no compatibility row|compatibility row|activateStandalone|standalone skill\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor --glob '*.md' | head -30\"}"},"time":{"start":1794529393696,"end":1794529394991}}}}
