{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794529487546,"sessionID":"ses_e2db80179ffeaOrYcgpmM7vbPY","part":{"partID":"prt_1d24ae89d002w2DAM6bdOcg110","sessionID":"ses_e2db80179ffeaOrYcgpmM7vbPY","messageID":"msg_1d24ae0f1001JvtieJ0hoEELKC","type":"tool","id":"call_48f3b9527a664e05abb575ae","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/scratch/briefs/wC.txt"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/scratch/briefs/wC.txt, lines 1-37\n1: REPOSITORY ROOT: /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\n2: Every read, write and command uses this root. Your environment block may name a different\n3: \"Workspace root folder\": ignore it, it is another checkout of the same repository.\n4: \n5: GATE 3 IS PRE-RESOLVED. DO NOT ASK THE DOCUMENTATION-SCOPE QUESTION.\n6: \n7: You are a non-interactive dispatched worker. `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` and\n8: `SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_ENFORCE=0` are set in your environment, which this repository's AGENTS.md\n9: defines as the autonomous child-dispatch exemption: the spec-folder question is pre-resolved\n10: and MUST NOT be asked. No answer can reach you, because nobody is at a prompt.\n11: \n12: Your write authority is already bound. The spec folder is:\n13:   specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach\n14: \n15: Proceed directly to the work. Do not print A/B/C/D options. Do not stop to confirm anything.\n16: A failed edit match means a stale anchor: re-read the file and retry; halt only after three\n17: failures on the same file.\n18: Your task is complete only when files exist on disk and the verification command has been run.\n19: \n20: PERSONA: You are the @code implementer, a LEAF worker dispatched by an orchestrator (Depth: 1).\n21: Edit exactly the one file this brief names. Never dispatch another agent or CLI, never run pi.\n22: Never commit, push or touch git state. Touch no other file. Verify before you report.\n23: Report: the file written, the verify output, and anything you could not do.\n24: \n25: TASK: edit ONE file, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts`. Read it in full, then `scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs` (functions `metadataEntries`, `standaloneCommandRecords`, `activateStandaloneCommands`, `standaloneRuntimeRow`, `renderTypescriptBridge`, `main`), `scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json` and `scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json`.\n26: \n27: Background: three legacy command bridge ids were retired from the advisor. `memory:save` and `command-memory-save` are replaced by ONE id `command-speckit-save` (the `/speckit:save` command). The umbrella id `command-spec-kit` (for `/spec_kit`) is gone: a typed `/speckit:plan` now returns `command-spec-kit-plan`, `/speckit:resume` returns `command-spec-kit-resume`, and so on, one id per command. `command-prompt-improver` (`/prompt`) is replaced by `command-prompt-improve` (`/prompt:improve`). The slash command `/memory:save` no longer exists as a command file. The TypeScript scorer was already updated.\n28: \n29: What changed in the generator, which this guard test must now hold instead of the old shape:\n30: - `allow-list.json` has 4 rows (was 8).\n31: - A command of a standalone skill (a skill folder with `command-metadata.json` and no `mode-registry.json`: `system-spec-kit` and `sk-prompt`) is active in both scorers by construction, with a generated row when `scoring-compatibility.json` has no hand row. Its phrases come from `userIntent.ownedSignals` in the metadata.\n32: - `metadataEntries` now also returns `description`, `ownedSignals`, `standalone` and `mutating`, and each generated TypeScript bridge carries `ownerSkill`.\n33: - So the active non-doctor TypeScript rows are no longer exactly the 5 hand-written ones, and the Python rows are no longer exactly 15.\n34: \n35: Three tests fail: \"generated projection exactly equals JSON-derived ids union the residual allow-list and the doctor routes\", \"generates all inventory ids for both runtimes while scoring only the compatibility snapshots\" and \"preserves the Python bridge records, order, and owner normalization byte-for-byte\". Rewrite their expectations so each still guards its intent against the NEW rule: derive the expected values from the same source files the generator reads (hand rows from `scoring-compatibility.json`, plus one generated row per standalone-skill command that has no hand row), never from a hard-coded count copied from the current output. Keep every assertion that still holds. Do not edit the generator or any other file. If the test compares against a constant in `lib/scorer/projection.ts` named `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGES` that is now out of date, do NOT edit that file: report exactly what in it is stale.\n36: \n37: VERIFY from `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`: `npx vitest run tests/command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed. Then prove the guard still bites: delete one phrase from a `/speckit:save` row inside the generated block of `lib/scorer/projection.ts` by hand, run the test (it must fail), then restore the file with `node scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs` and confirm `--check` prints `fresh`. Report both runs.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/scratch/briefs/wC.txt, lines 1-37\n1: REPOSITORY ROOT: /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/