ks: an ask-first reason always wins, a doctor route\n487-// that mutates asks because its repair is the operator's call, and only a\n488-// read-only route or an add-only route confined to the spec folder may run\n489-// unprompted. Everything else starts as an ordinary task.\n490-function derivePolicy(record) {\n491-  if (Array.isArray(record.ask_first) && record.ask_first.length > 0) return 'ask';\n492-  if (record.doctor === true && record.mutating === 'mutates') return 'ask';\n493-  if (record.mutating === 'read-only') return 'run';\n494-  if (record.mutating === 'add-only' && record.write_scope === 'spec-folder') return 'run';\n495-  return 'start';\n496-}\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"456:function validateRiskKeys(record, label, requireTarget = false) {\n457-  if (!MUTATING_CLASSES.includes(record.mutating)) {\n458-    throw new Error(\n459-      `[command-bridges] ${label} has mutating ${JSON.stringify(record.mutating)}; `\n460-        + `expected one of ${MUTATING_CLASSES.join(', ')}`,\n461-    );\n462-  }\n463-  if (record.ask_first !== undefined) {\n464-    const askFirst = record.ask_first;\n465-    if (!Array.isArray(askFirst) || askFirst.some((value) => !ASK_FIRST_REASONS.includes(value))) {\n466-      throw new Error(\n467-        `[command-bridges] ${label} has ask_first ${JSON.stringify(askFirst)}; `\n468-          + `expected an array of ${ASK_FIRST_REASONS.join(', ')}`,\n469-      );\n470-    }\n471-  }\n472-  if (record.write_scope !== undefined && !WRITE_SCOPES.includes(record.write_scope)) {\n473-    throw new Error(\n474-      `[command-bridges] ${label} has write_scope ${JSON.stringify(record.write_scope)}; `\n475-        + `expected one of ${WRITE_SCOPES.join(', ')}`,\n476-    );\n477-  }\n478-  if (requireTarget && (typeof record.gate3_location !== 'string' || !record.gate3_location)) {\n479-    throw new Error(\n480-      `[command-bridges] ${label} needs a non-empty string gate3_location naming what it writes`,\n481-    );\n482-  }\n483-}\n484-\n485-// One policy per command, decided from the risk keys alone so the answer never\n486-// depends on which scorer asks: an ask-first reason always wins, a doctor route\n487-// that mutates asks because its repair is the operator's call, and only a\n488-// read-only route or an add-only route confined to the spec folder may run\n489-// unprompted. Everything else starts as an ordinary task.\n490-function derivePolicy(record) {\n491-  if (Array.isArray(record.ask_first) && record.ask_first.length > 0) return 'ask';\n492-  if (record.doctor === true && record.mutating === 'mutates') return 'ask';\n493-  if (record.mutating === 'read-only') return 'run';\n494-  if (record.mutating === 'add-only' && record.write_scope === 'spec-folder') return 'run';\n495-  return 'start';\n496-}\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \\\"function validateRiskKeys\\\" -A 40 .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794529530360,"end":1794529530935}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794529530943,"sessionID":"ses_e2db80179ffeaOrYcgpmM7vbPY","part":{"partID":"prt_1d24b8ef50015v69LdI1aern34","sessionID":"ses_e2db80179ffeaOrYcgpmM7vbPY","messageID":"msg_1d24b214d001zb4jwjoVGFUcu5","type":"tool","id":"call_b9c59618ac0249958832507f","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \"CARRY|compatibility row|fixture|deriver\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md | head -40"},"output":"3:description: \"Generate one command table from the bridge deriver, fill four recommendation fields from it, print the command and its policy in the brief head, state the degraded contract and retire the allow-list and the hand-authored leftovers. Prove it with a schema test, six golden briefs and the unchanged floors.\"\n23:| **Language/Stack** | TypeScript on Node, one CommonJS deriver, the Python fallback scorer |\n29:The deriver already knows each command's runnable string, policy and owner. It now writes them into one generated table in `command-attach.ts`, and the handler, the CLI fallback, the degraded path and the renderer all read that table. The brief head gains the command and its policy. A schema test and six golden briefs prove the contract. The pinned captures prove nothing else moved.\n39:- [x] The operator keeps the CARRY-003 group (\"Carry three, settle five (Recommended)\").\n65:`command-metadata.json`, `_routes.yaml` and the projection feed the deriver, which writes `commandPolicies` and the new table. At recommend time the scorer ranks rows and the handler copies the fields from the table. The CLI passes them to the hook. The renderer prints the head from the fields, or from the table when a field is missing.\n93:| `rankShippedFleet` | Hit only on an exact hub id | Also hit on an owned command row | Reach fixture tests and the live check |\n94:| `allow-list.json` and its reader in the deriver | Four legacy ids | Delete | `--check` counts with no `allowList` key |\n95:| Gold and fixture labels | Name the four old ids | Relabel by script | `scratch/relabel-list.txt` and the pinned capture |\n107:Setup records the before numbers, the live brief heads, the reach check, the hook timing and the suite. Implementation waits for the phase 007 confirmation, then runs the waves in `tasks.md`: the table, the fields, the head, the degraded contract, the reach check, the tests, the id retirement, the `nm-sk-doc-01` fix and the CARRY-003 group. Verification rebuilds, reruns every floor, the CLI checks, the brief heads, the reach check with real embeddings and the suite, then fills the summary.\n117:| Unit | Schema fields, the six golden heads, the renderer matrix, the degraded contract, the older-daemon render, the reach check fixtures, the activation fixture | Vitest in `ADV` and `node` on the sk-doc reach test file |\n172:The operator answered the four design questions on 2026-11-12, each with the recommended option: \"Rename the four, drop /prompt (Recommended)\", \"Only a typed command (Recommended)\", \"The strictest: ask (Recommended)\" and \"No (Recommended)\". The same day the operator kept CARRY-003 in this phase, moved the `nm-sk-doc-01` fix here (\"Fix it in phase 005 (Recommended)\") and set phase 007's before-measurement first (\"Now, on today's branch tip (Recommended)\"). `spec.md` section 10 holds each answer.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3:description: \"Generate one command table from the bridge deriver, fill four recommendation fields from it, print the command and its policy in the brief head, state the degraded contract and retire the allow-list and the hand-authored leftovers. Prove it with a schema test, six golden briefs and the unchanged floors.\"\n23:| **Language/Stack** | TypeScript on Node, one CommonJS deriver, the Python fallback scorer |\n29:The deriver already knows each command's runnable string, policy and owner. It now writes them into one generated table in `command-attach.ts`, and the handler, the CLI fallback, the degraded path and the renderer all read that table. The brief head gains the command and its policy. A schema test and six golden briefs prove the contract. The pinned captures prove nothing else moved.\n39:- [x] The operator keeps the CARRY-003 group (\"Carry three, settle five (Recommended)\").\n65:`command-metadata.json`, `_routes.yaml` and the projection feed the deriver, which writes `commandPolicies` and the new table. At recommend time the scorer ranks rows and the handler copies the fields from the table. The CLI passes them to the hook. The renderer prints the head from the fields, or from the table when a field is missing.\n93:| `rankShippedFleet` | Hit only on an exact hub id | Also hit on an owned command row | Reach fixture tests and the live check |\n94:| `allow-list.json` and its reader in the deriver | Four legacy ids | Delete | `--check` counts with no `allowList` key |\n95:| Gold and fixture labels | Name the four old ids | Relabel by script | `scratch/relabel-list.txt` and the pinned capture |\n107:Setup records the before numbers, the live brief heads, the reach check, the hook timing and the suite. Implementation waits for the phase 007 confirmation, then runs the waves in `tasks.md`: the table, the fields, the head, the degraded contract, the reach check, the tests, the id retirement, the `nm-sk-doc-01` fix and the CARRY-003 group. Verification rebuilds, reruns every floor, the CLI checks, the brief heads, the reach check with real embeddings and the suite, then fills the summary.\n117:| Unit | Schema fields, the six golden heads, the renderer matrix, the degraded contract, the older-daemon render, the reach check fixtures, the activation fixture | Vitest in `ADV` and `node` on the sk-doc reach test file |\n172:The operator answered the four design questions on 2026-11-12, each with the recommended option: \"Rename the four, drop /prompt (Recommended)\", \"Only a typed command (Recommended)\", \"The strictest: ask (Recommended)\" and \"No (Recommended)\". The same day the operator kept CARRY-003 in this phase, moved the `nm-sk-doc-01` fix here (\"Fix it in phase 005 (Recommended)\") and set phase 007's before-measurement first (\"Now, on today's branch tip (Recommended)\"). `spec.md` section 10 holds each answer.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \\\"CARRY|compatibility row|fixture|deriver\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1794529529589,"end":1794529530943}}}}
