{"type":"text","timestamp":1794529794279,"sessionID":"ses_e2db80179ffeaOrYcgpmM7vbPY","part":{"id":"prt_1d24f8805001BHpKzxxElBXb40","sessionID":"ses_e2db80179ffeaOrYcgpmM7vbPY","messageID":"msg_1d24f7ff0001eetkT7u1tD0al8","type":"text","text":"**Task T042 complete.** The line read: *CARRY-003 (b): add a fixture case in `$ADV/tests/command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts` for a standalone skill whose declared command `scoring-compatibility.json` does not list, asserting the derived entry is enabled for `typescript` and `python`.*\n\n## Files written (1)\n\n`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts`\n\n- Added one test case: `activates a standalone metadata command with no compatibility row in both runtimes`.\n- It builds a fixture through the file's existing `createFixtureRoot()`/`writeFile()` seam, writes one standalone skill (`gamma`, no `mode-registry.json`) declaring `/gamma:one` plus its risk keys and owned signals.\n- The activation rule lives only in the deriver's `main()` and no exported helper exposes it, so the case stages the folder layout the deriver resolves from its own location in the temp root and executes the **real** deriver (`execFileSync`, `NODE_PATH` at `.skilled/node_modules` for `yaml`). The fixture compatibility file has empty `typescript`/`python` lists, so no hand row can enable the command.\n- Asserts `standalone: true`, `runtime.typescript.enabled: true`, `runtime.python.enabled: true`.\n- Bite checked: with a `mode-registry.json` added to the fixture skill, the same run yields `standalone:false, ts:false, py:false`, so the assertions do catch a broken activation.\n\nNo other file was edited, no deriver change was needed, and the T042 checkbox in `tasks.md` was left unticked.\n\n## Verify output\n\nFrom `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`:\n\n```\n RUN  v4.1.12 /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  9 passed (9)\n```\n\n0 failed. Also ran `npm run typecheck` in the same directory: exit 0, no output. The added diff contains no spec path, task id, ADR/REQ id, or CARRY label.","time":{"start":1794529789957,"end":1794529794279}}}
